.TH IDAPTIK-LAUNCHER 1 "November 2026" "IDApTIK 0.5.0" "Player Commands"
.SH NAME
idaptik-launcher \- diagnose, repair, build, and launch IDApTIK solo or multiplayer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./launcher.sh
.RI [ mode ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The IDApTIK launcher is the canonical player entry point.  With no arguments
it opens a menu for solo play, multiplayer hosting/joining, status, and
diagnostics.  Every launch performs a fail-closed runtime preflight before it
builds or starts a relay.  It then prints a tick/cross startup checklist and
does not declare readiness merely because a process exists.
.SH PLAYER MODES
.TP
.B --solo
Build and open the Bevy GUI with both roles controlled locally.
.TP
.BR --host " [--role infiltrator|hacker]"
Check host dependencies and route, build the GUI, start and health-check the
Phoenix/Bandit relay, then open the selected seat.  Invite another player only
after the green READY FOR JOINERS message.
.TP
.BR --join " HOST [--role infiltrator|hacker]"
Check the join machine, build the GUI, and probe HOST port 4000.  The client
does not start until the relay answers.  HOST may be a name, IPv4 address,
host:port pair, or ws:// / wss:// URL.
.TP
.BR --auto , " --browser" , " --web"
Open the interactive menu.  This is the default.
.TP
.B --windows-client
A modifier for --solo, --host, --join and --auto: build and run the native
Windows Bevy client instead of the WSLg one.  Windows interop is discovered at
/mnt/c/Windows/System32 (or the drvfs root reported by wslpath), so cmd.exe does
not need to be on PATH, and interop is proved by executing cmd.exe rather than
by trusting that the file exists.  Provision it with
.B just windows-client-deps
(the x86_64-pc-windows-gnu target and the MinGW cross-linker).  The relay and
Tailscale endpoint stay in WSL.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS AND REPAIR
.TP
.B --doctor
Print machine, OS/kernel/architecture, WSL/WSLg transport, CPU/memory,
graphics coprocessor/renderer, audio, pinned Rust and Elixir dependencies,
Tailscale, and host-route status.  Fatal checks return non-zero.
.TP
.B --repair
Trust the repository and install its pinned mise dependencies.  On WSL2 NAT,
offer guided Tailscale installation/authentication.  Host-level WSLg recovery
is explained but never performed automatically because wsl --shutdown would
terminate every active WSL process.
.TP
.B --flowdiags
Open the static HTML launch/troubleshooting flowchart.  Under WSL it uses the
Windows browser so it remains usable when WSLg windows are broken.
.TP
.B --man
Display this manual.
.SH LIFECYCLE MODES
.TP
.B --start
Alias for solo GUI launch.
.TP
.B --status
Report tracked game/relay processes, binary state, and logs.
.TP
.B --stop
Stop the tracked game and relay.
.TP
.BR --integ " [--force]"
Install desktop/start-menu integration.
.TP
.B --disinteg
Remove integration while preserving configuration and logs.
.SH RENDERER EVIDENCE
Readiness means the client process started; it does not say what draws the
frame.  After a solo launch the launcher reads the AdapterInfo line Bevy logs
when it selects an adapter and prints it, for example:
.PP
.nf
renderer: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Laptop GPU (Vulkan)
.fi
.PP
A software adapter (llvmpipe, softpipe, SwiftShader, WARP) is reported as
WARNING and named as software, because a successful build on the CPU renderer
looks identical to a successful build on the GPU until the frame rate gives it
away.  --status prints the same line from the last run's log.  The doctor
reports both the OpenGL renderer (glxinfo) and the adapter Bevy actually
selected; these can disagree.
.SH READINESS CONTRACT
The host's READY FOR JOINERS message means runtime diagnostics passed, the GUI
build completed, the relay answered its health probe, a peer-reachable address
exists, and the host seat is launching.  The joiner's READY -- JOINING HOST NOW
message means its diagnostics/build passed and the exact host relay answered.
A warning is a degradation; a cross is blocking and nothing should launch.
.SH WSLG COPY MODE
If Windows shows a penguin taskbar item prefixed [WARN: COPY MODE], WSLg failed
its shared-memory window transport.  The launcher detects the Weston
rdp_allocate_shared_memory error or missing /mnt/shared_memory.  When Windows
interop, the x86_64-pc-windows-gnu Rust target, and the MinGW linker are
available, it bypasses WSLg with a native Windows Bevy client while retaining
the Phoenix relay and Tailscale endpoint in WSL.  Otherwise it stops before
launch.  The same client can be requested explicitly with --windows-client when
WSLg opens a window that dies during surface or present-mode negotiation; the
launcher prints that command when it sees the client die that early.  In Windows PowerShell as Administrator run:
.PP
.nf
wsl --update
wsl --shutdown
.fi
.PP
Reopen the distribution and run --doctor.  Restart Windows if necessary.  Do
not manually create /mnt/shared_memory; WSLg must supply the host-backed mount.
.SH NETWORKING
WSL2 NAT addresses in 172.16.0.0/12 are not offered to peers.  Tailscale is the
supported simple route and must be connected before the host becomes ready.
The joiner probes the selected host and port before launching.
.SH EXTENDED COPROCESSORS
QPU, APU, IOPU, vector, physics, math, tensor, neural, graphics, and crypto
suite work is separate architecture planning.  Except for the graphics adapter
needed by Bevy, that suite is not a runtime dependency of this release and the
doctor does not claim those backends are implemented.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IDAPTIK_PORT
Relay port; default 4000.
.TP
.B IDAPTIK_REPO_DIR
Override the repository located by an integrated launcher.
.TP
.B IDAPTIK_STARTUP_TIMEOUT
Maximum seconds to wait for readiness; default 1800.
.TP
.B IDAPTIK_RENDERER_WAIT
Seconds a solo launch waits for Bevy's adapter line before reporting that the
log has none yet; default 6.
.TP
.B IDAPTIK_CLIENT_PLATFORM
linux or windows.  --windows-client sets it; an explicit value wins over the
WSLg Copy Mode fallback, but is still validated against WSL2/interop.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/idaptik/game.log
GUI/build startup log.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/idaptik/startup.progress
Machine-readable startup phase stream.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/idaptik/startup.ready
Readiness record, created only after all startup gates.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/idaptik-multiplayer/relay.log
Phoenix/Bandit relay log.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the requested report/action completed.  Diagnostics and launches
return non-zero for blocking faults, failed builds, unreachable relays, or
readiness timeout.  Warnings alone do not fail.
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/MULTIPLAYER-TROUBLESHOOTING.md, docs/player-launch-flow.html
